{"title":"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Very_Thorough)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Very Thorough)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(Very_much_overkill,_but_fast_if_you_know_stuff)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (Very much overkill, but fast if you know stuff)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(faster_version_of_solution_1,_less_technical_than_solution_5)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (faster version of solution 1, less technical than solution 5)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_MOP_2024\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by MOP 2024</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> be the unique function defined on the positive integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/7/b5732e957114ff62dabd6b1f9c816210038356c0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{d\\mid n}d\\cdot f\\left(\\frac{n}{d}\\right)=1\\]\" width=\"133\" height=\"45\" /> for all positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86b66b16facae2fb5d875d9b2ea67deeef9f3dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2023)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/8/5080b0cc81367d7a45480888a6a6bec48376d206.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}~-1536\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}~96\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}~108\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}~116\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}~144$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"464\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Very_Thorough.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Very_Thorough)\">Solution 1 (Very Thorough)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Very Thorough)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/d/b6dd0ff40babd7fbd0c3e3d3b019627c27949616.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(1) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"66\" height=\"18\" />, since the only divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> is itself.   \n</p><p><br />\nThen, let's look at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/e/3ee4d848be5a5de8e4a59a62b13f783619e92c0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> a prime. We see that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f559fdd288189b05531f43dc25598b40bf1ba2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{d \\mid p} d \\cdot f\\left(\\frac{p}{d}\\right) = 1\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"45\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/8/f18505ba942a8c6483a174d1cac33d5d2eb7d216.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 \\cdot f(p) + p \\cdot f(1) = 1\\]\" width=\"165\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/d/04ddc013a6e6e26e770465e71194d12eadae9099.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(p) = 1 - p \\cdot f(1)\\]\" width=\"143\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/3/2a3e5f0b0a9c5c595c19e071709629891693dcca.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(p) = 1-p\\]\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />\nNice.   \n</p><p>Now consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/8/1b8b042a20f1fb01ebb3ddc30ed136da4f1641b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p^k)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"22\" />, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/767a53f43be056f9333f71e3e39f59aa0f8bca35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\in \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/b/60b24baac79f71fed4253ebd5ec43a0a3dd7b286.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{d \\mid p^k} d \\cdot f\\left(\\frac{p^k}{d}\\right) = 1\\]\" width=\"144\" height=\"51\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/b/63b847b760837b74f35f836232edf7d66c127bb1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 \\cdot f(p^k) + p \\cdot f(p^{k-1}) + p^2 \\cdot f(p^{k-2}) + \\dotsc + p^k f(1) = 1\\]\" width=\"427\" height=\"20\" />.  \n</p><p><br />\nIt can be (strongly) inductively shown that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/b/42b1d99f9d09cb0d070094a198584c7ddc14bd87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p^k) = f(p) = 1-p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"167\" height=\"22\" />. Here's how.    \n</p><p>We already showed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> works. Suppose it holds for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/5/d35a51f5f4479cf610e903ad871c5baa6f1fe9c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = n$\" width=\"45\" height=\"12\" />, then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/6/396c12e3c58d13a6c50ce3911634bc7163641f7e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 \\cdot f(p^n) + p \\cdot f(p^{n-1}) + p^2 \\cdot f(p^{n-2}) + \\dotsc + p^n f(1) = 1 \\implies f(p^m) = 1-p \\; \\forall \\; m \\leqslant n\\]\" width=\"599\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/2/522d2a0cff1cea5a57526bee66d7187cf8d9e83d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" />, we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/a/bfa01db67345f871695d4661d0c0259fd0ea097a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 \\cdot f(p^{n+1}) + p \\cdot f(p^{n}) + p^2 \\cdot f(p^{n-1}) + \\dotsc + p^{n+1} f(1) = 1\\]\" width=\"447\" height=\"20\" />, then using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/4/8e4b0954b5b73473a58e62726ce151e167c5a57c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(p^m) = 1-p \\; \\forall \\; m \\leqslant n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"184\" height=\"20\" />, we simplify to\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/0/29077dfb707f70b3bf9b40c86b61dd1ce9ef8b50.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 \\cdot f(p^{n+1}) + p \\cdot (1-p) + p^2 \\cdot (1-p) + \\dotsc + p^n \\cdot (1-p) + p^{n+1} f(1) = 1\\]\" width=\"537\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e85bc6d570ab32bd081b6d224ffd025d424efb33.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(p^{n+1}) + \\sum_{i=1}^n p^i (1-p) + p^{n+1} = 1\\]\" width=\"269\" height=\"47\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/d/d9df6e3cdf5f9a31bd88c82367403d67aebb7bc5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(p^{n+1}) + p(1 - p^n) + p^{n+1} = 1\\]\" width=\"244\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/0/4f0dc7b7b19128a981c8baa47a201d5b5bbb3908.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(p^{n+1}) + p = 1 \\implies f(p^{n+1}) = 1-p\\]\" width=\"298\" height=\"20\" />.   \n</p><p>Very nice! Now, we need to show that this function is multiplicative, i.e. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/9/5a936c67de9bf90a62b57652f27c11a1b63a780c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(pq) = f(p) \\cdot f(q)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"150\" height=\"20\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/e/03e38c129ca913b528941c02d331db303e078a2c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{distinct}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"65\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f779d95c15f7e41de74cb767f52fe4e7b92c745e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p,q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"13\" /> prime.\nIt's pretty standard, let's go through it quickly.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/9/979ffbb62d1315cc258c9b6952d71619938671f8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{d \\mid pq} d \\cdot f\\left(\\frac{pq}{d}\\right) = 1\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"45\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/5/2d5dcbb52484d1fd2f74044ced9344b114749eb7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 \\cdot f(pq) + p \\cdot f(q) + q \\cdot f(p) + pq \\cdot f(1) = 1\\]\" width=\"339\" height=\"18\" />\nUsing our formulas from earlier, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/a/0fae8dd189fa8e125f0bae0d1219d6070697fde9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(pq) + p(1-q) + q(1-p) + pq = 1 \\implies f(pq) = 1 - p(1-q) - q(1-p) - pq = (1-p)(1-q) = f(p) \\cdot f(q)\\]\" width=\"756\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Great! We're almost done now. \nLet's actually plug in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/b/42b039f5f964ef25f21a18450c773a1a6ddbdc87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023 = 7 \\cdot 17^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"110\" height=\"17\" /> into the original formula. \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/a/dda154ced07e59ffaac456728d9ae471ca641519.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{d \\mid 2023} d \\cdot f\\left(\\frac{2023}{d}\\right) = 1\\]\" width=\"175\" height=\"50\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/9/7a9c37232f9609b7e2914e500499b326a1f41a34.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 \\cdot f(2023) + 7 \\cdot f(17^2) + 17 \\cdot f(7 \\cdot 17) + 7 \\cdot 17 \\cdot f(17) + 17^2 \\cdot f(7) + 7 \\cdot 17^2 \\cdot f(1) = 1\\]\" width=\"546\" height=\"20\" />\nLet's use our formulas! We know \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/9/329891a35dda3a5631a661e79e9b0f936e503216.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(7) = 1-7 = -6\\]\" width=\"145\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/1/c51ae9b8db41a6e3a29b6dbd98459d7738893e8c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(17) = 1-17 = -16\\]\" width=\"172\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/6/91631b7da9c8daa7ea0e310250ca990162bbf37d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(7 \\cdot 17) = f(7) \\cdot f(17) = (-6) \\cdot (-16) = 96\\]\" width=\"342\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/d/2cd6eb7c66bfd8ccec829e7c06b43b704127d7db.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(17^2) = f(17) = -16\\]\" width=\"173\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>So plugging ALL that in, we have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/7/c47de0bc24769d3cac2257c27180164424fb926b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(2023) = 1 - \\left(7 \\cdot (-16) + 17 \\cdot (-6) \\cdot (-16) + 7 \\cdot 17 \\cdot (-16) + 17^2 \\cdot (-6) + 7 \\cdot 17^2\\right)\\]\" width=\"632\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>which, be my guest simplifying, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/1/591cc5e0edfb3ca7326582a3093060eca5e7e493.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} \\ 96}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~ <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/8/b38096ce59206eb4c0d50fb9b38f89ef03c30ee0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\color{magenta} zoomanTV$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"93\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, change the problem into an easier form.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/1/b41e422e6b54d65bb9e78957d3b43fd8f7569e09.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{d\\mid n}d\\cdot f(\\frac{n}{d} )=\\sum_{d\\mid n}\\frac{n}{d}f(d)=1\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"44\" />\nSo now we get \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/9/d594b233a7bf670778b759532ec0fb5feab366a0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{1}{n}= \\sum_{d\\mid n}\\frac{f(d)}{d}\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"50\" />\nAlso, notice that both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/e/10ead85194dd8035f5df7266b2aa16c1eea52b6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{f(d)}{d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"40\" height=\"40\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/d/83dacecc3f852b6d1fc31accf43e249930c0b27f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"13\" height=\"37\" /> are arithmetic functions. Applying Möbius inversion formula, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/02763be61d8434986782f0965e6496dc4cc15f48.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{f(n)}{n}=\\sum_{d\\mid n}\\frac{ \\mu (d) }{\\frac{n}{d} }=\\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{d\\mid n}d\\cdot \\mu (d)\\]\" width=\"256\" height=\"50\" />\nSo \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/9/7e93bc291a4e502a291084b285c9e1c109426dbd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(n)=1-p_1-p_2-...+p_1p_2+...=(1-p_1)(1-p_2)...=\\prod_{p\\mid n}(1-p)\\]\" width=\"537\" height=\"41\" />\nSo the answer should be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/4/ac432894172349530f740cf74adf5d1ff53afe19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2023)=\\prod_{p\\mid 2023}(1-p)=(1-7)(1-17)=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} \\ 96}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -27px\" width=\"409\" height=\"47\" />\n</p><p>~ZZZIIIVVV\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the problem, we want to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86b66b16facae2fb5d875d9b2ea67deeef9f3dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2023)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />. Using the problem, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/c/bdc5c6003fc428386a67e01f5d777a93c8b31da7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2023)+7f(289)+17f(119)+119f(17)+289f(7)+2023f(1)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"542\" height=\"20\" />. By plugging in factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/0873e9fed23538e535ac05c3284b86bd7bce6fd6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf3caffae8a8ce96550be80b0e7e46279818e3f2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align} f(7)+7f(1)=1\\\\ f(17)+17f(1)=1\\\\ f(119)+7f(17)+17f(7)+119f(1)=1\\\\ f(289)+17f(17)+289f(1)=1 \\end{align}\" width=\"427\" height=\"93\" />\nNotice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/9/c695bb36878f2328df441254ba310bab1eab66d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4)-17(2)=f(289)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/0/b50c60bffcb0f1db36e7c4180717f8c5f37297b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(289)=-16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"111\" height=\"20\" />. Similarly, notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/e/47ee42564f3f0d4129bd595eebb0acac5b466da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)-17(1)=f(119)+7f(17)=-16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"296\" height=\"20\" />. Now, substituting this all back into our equation to solve for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/6/b86b66b16facae2fb5d875d9b2ea67deeef9f3dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2023)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />, we get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/d/66d2aaeb6619ff250fd835d5871daba812358f1a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} f(2023)+7f(289)+17(f(119)+7f(17))+289(f(7)+7f(1))=1\\\\ f(2023)+7 \\cdot (-16) + 17 \\cdot (-16) + 289 \\cdot (1) = 1\\\\ f(2023)=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)} \\ 96} \\end{align*}\" width=\"522\" height=\"79\" />\n-PhunsukhWangdu\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/4/404d04c4b7baeb72ad540e86184a1f2c43d2fdaa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\in \\Bbb N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" /> with prime factorization <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/4/4d464d146320d3b23bda7c60b60b1c17cb6b5324.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\Pi_{i=1}^k p_i^{\\alpha_i}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"97\" height=\"22\" />.\nThus, the equation given in this problem can be equivalently written as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c05f583b0527e7d8b16292db1a1b6f75a77f6a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ \\sum_{\\beta_1 = 0}^{\\alpha_1} \\sum_{\\beta_2 = 0}^{\\alpha_2} \\cdots \\sum_{\\beta_k = 0}^{\\alpha_k} \\Pi_{i=1}^k p_i^{\\alpha_i - \\beta_i} \\cdot f \\left( \\Pi_{i=1}^k p_i^{\\beta_i} \\right) = 1 . \\]\" width=\"353\" height=\"50\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/8/ea8029abe8dfc03855b2ce0eb13e173b92380120.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\noindent \\textbf{Special case 1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"17\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/6/c766f9fce6070981e62f805a7cf7294baed4498e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/a/1fa184e087a9a12209193183369505960c78295f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f \\left( 1 \\right) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/e/93e107dc9c3d46d43704d18932573a1dce8885aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\noindent \\textbf{Special case 2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"17\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a prime.\n</p><p>We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb7e1936c7369e70f4c2bc980fdd93eda4566bb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ 1 \\cdot f \\left( n \\right) + n \\cdot f \\left( 1 \\right) = 1 . \\]\" width=\"180\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/0/a10d3ab763dabd0ae5c88fc9b3095f2a6007e796.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f \\left( n \\right) = 1 - n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/e/61e0fe43af9ce4b00ff24b65f0b375d7f8942097.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\noindent \\textbf{Special case 3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"17\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is the square of a prime, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/d/cadc49b7bc0a9753fab92e59b21a950c2090dc46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = p_1^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"54\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/d/bdd5231bc6c2e889acca10444e4cf9a99fd0887a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ 1 \\cdot f \\left( p_1^2 \\right) + p_1 \\cdot f \\left( p_1 \\right) + p_1^2 \\cdot f \\left( 1 \\right) = 1. \\]\" width=\"290\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/2/842211f30b6925c7e8b70636ab1d479f447e8869.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f \\left( p_1^2 \\right) = 1 - p_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"121\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/16357b1b5c4effd97d8f112869ff3510542cb0f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\noindent \\textbf{Special case 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"17\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is the product of two distinct primes, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/b/3cb37c0194a3542f84513bf6df8f8cb9a1b569e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = p_1 p_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/d/85d71a3c22be5949ce46c31a0089a93c6c56d9e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ 1 \\cdot f \\left( p_1 p_2 \\right) + p_1 \\cdot f \\left( p_2 \\right) + p_2 \\cdot f \\left( p_1 \\right) + p_1 p_2 \\cdot f \\left( 1 \\right) = 1. \\]\" width=\"417\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/a/b3a09d699ecac6a4331c7cf69cb73c2fdd2d205a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f \\left( p_1 p_2 \\right) = 1 - p_1 - p_2 + p_1 p_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"229\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/a/c6a87041aef75c9eccb209d1dff677e0167a3ba5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\noindent \\textbf{Special case 5}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"117\" height=\"17\" />: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> takes the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/9/0a954e4176396b90c9565b2e8688021c045434be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = p_1^2 p_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"70\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/1/e01486dcc7cb25518b89692706b17389dc67c92b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"15\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/e/a2e8bc2235f5b0094bc37f2ef74f7dc647f0a406.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> are two distinct primes.\n</p><p>We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/d/d4de58060d0a321f25435fe47fd9cf113c648bb5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ 1 \\cdot f \\left( p_1^2 p_2 \\right) + p_1 \\cdot f \\left( p_1 p_2 \\right) + p_1^2 \\cdot f \\left( p_2 \\right) + p_2 \\cdot f \\left( p_1^2 \\right) + p_1 p_2 f \\left( p_1 \\right) + p_1^2 p_2 f \\left( 1 \\right) = 1. \\]\" width=\"549\" height=\"21\" />\n</p><p>Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/b/a2b3af0fc3796cb2227ff8e39d2bf3dc2272f9d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f \\left( p_1^2 p_2 \\right) = 1 - p_1 - p_2 + p_1 p_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -7px\" width=\"232\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p>The prime factorization of 2023 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/7/b2763bc0769d8e0f36017537e9772fe256889552.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\cdot 17^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"17\" />.\nTherefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/c/1bc57d1cfa2307f6c899164122cfbf2da233debf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} f \\left( 2023 \\right) &amp; = 1 - 7 - 17 + 7 \\cdot 17 \\\\ &amp; = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) 96}}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"231\" height=\"54\" />\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28Very_much_overkill.2C_but_fast_if_you_know_stuff.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(Very_much_overkill,_but_fast_if_you_know_stuff)\">Solution 5 (Very much overkill, but fast if you know stuff)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (Very much overkill, but fast if you know stuff)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the below, denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/8/878f37474d8c8584e1ad5794356964a2f281fc43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{id}(x)=x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/e/2becd15586bbd15f2dce1e1ebd5447484d75b70d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1(x)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"69\" height=\"20\" />, and let the Dirichlet convolution of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/1/311cabda3a9b09f0dde217303ca9d1cd9201dcf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/2/80251052bc580cb7077eaf6c36cf424111546d29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f*g$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"37\" height=\"16\" />. Denote the Dirichlet inverse of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/1/74153d34ed1e2096b5c034cb85eff5a695b887c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" />. Also, let the Dirichlet series of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> evaluated at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/7/f37bba504894945c07a32f5496d74299a37aa51c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> be:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/2/e42186b0ade6ed79a477caa81e0fe8628d7ea0e2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[DG_f(s)=\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\frac{f(n)}{n^s}.\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"48\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/1/031cb95fe26028bb28c91f9ba046b40eca3bc5f1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\zeta(s)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> be the Riemann zeta function.\n</p><p>We note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/2/3c24a62ff224d7d033e74d6a804eec25c5e4f477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{d|n}{d\\cdot f\\left(\\frac{n}{d}\\right)}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -27px\" width=\"136\" height=\"48\" /> is equivalent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/c/05cda39ad0d023d2687fcc1ddd34525ce678258c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f=1*\\operatorname{id}^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"21\" />. We state a well-known theorem:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/c/13cadc6f5031a0045865ca70c2926199dd76ef61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[DG_f(s)DG_g(s)=DG_{f*g}(s)\\]\" width=\"218\" height=\"19\" />.\nBy this:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/4/2f44995e1585b5ebb4aedc437778659b0f4128f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[DG_{\\operatorname{id}^{-1}}(s)=\\frac{1}{DG_{\\operatorname{id}}(s)}=\\frac{1}{\\zeta(s-1)}.\\]\" width=\"267\" height=\"41\" />\nWe know also that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/d/d8d91a6fc55785de6ae74a97b1fad816c73a3a93.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\frac{\\mu(n)}{n^s}=\\frac{1}{\\zeta(s)}\\]\" width=\"126\" height=\"48\" />,\nso:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/4/524abf304837ec492684105fe90d981d5015bc48.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[DG_{\\operatorname{id}^{-1}}(s)=\\sum_{n=1}^{\\infty}\\frac{n\\mu(n)}{n^s},\\]\" width=\"187\" height=\"48\" />\ni.e., <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/5/56559d19657fa1cd158a8aa7f45d318d4e35518a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\operatorname{id}^{-1}(n)=n\\mu(n).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"136\" height=\"22\" /> Thus:\n\\begin{align*}\nf(2023)&amp;=\\left(\\operatorname{id}^{-1}*1\\right)(2023)\\\\\n&amp;=\\sum_{d|2023}{n\\mu(n)}\\\\\n&amp;=\\mu(1)+7\\mu(7)+17\\mu(17)+7\\cdot 17\\mu(7\\cdot 17)\\\\\n&amp;= 7\\cdot 17-7-17+1\\\\\n&amp;=96\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>Hence we choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/5/7a558b37c441e1b7ac7c5ff6a848f199ac53ba75.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"40\" height=\"29\" />.\n~Sivin\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28faster_version_of_solution_1.2C_less_technical_than_solution_5.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(faster_version_of_solution_1,_less_technical_than_solution_5)\">Solution 6 (faster version of solution 1, less technical than solution 5)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (faster version of solution 1, less technical than solution 5)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/0/9500554074a26b37ac8a419cb4682356005ffe17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(f\\star Id)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" /> be the dirichlet convolution of f,Id. As above, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/5/2652f1077d0dc6af12073a7217263c01e5d8b1dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Id(x) = x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"80\" height=\"20\" />.\nwe are given that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/5/025ad0570155f4b78c40887740b225a894d9d69a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(f\\star Id)(n) =\\sum_{d|n}f(\\frac{n}{d})Id(d)=\\sum_{d|n}f(\\frac{n}{d})(d)=1\\]\" width=\"368\" height=\"44\" /> for all n. Therefore:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/8/c484b3886adbae7a826e7d3c2f8ed676e451adf8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{d|1}f(\\frac{1}{d})(d)=1\\implies f(1)(1)=1 \\implies f(1) = 1\\]\" width=\"379\" height=\"49\" />\nNow, a good idea when you look at something like this is look at simple things. We have already covered with 1 divisor, now lets look at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/f/74fd85afeb25627a961382162e87d1969b921837.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" /> for 2 divisors.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/9/b79555fc2489a11a395d55f4f10597ca912e53f7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{d|n}f(\\frac{n}{d})(d)=1\\implies\\sum_{d|p}f(\\frac{p}{d})(d)=1\\implies 1*f(p) + p * f(1)=1\\]\" width=\"523\" height=\"44\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bacfaca054508fa7990b658310ab40f774962fb0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\because f(1)=1, f(p)+p=1\\implies f(p)=1-p\\]\" width=\"339\" height=\"18\" />\nNow, you could entirely skip the above step and that changes none of the rest, it is just a good idea to always check edge cases like this. Now, for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/6585024dc6db82bcfd717e03212be80536d94a83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"19\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/7/5370e0df45c2d43d3df3c08dd98966d99fc19f8a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(f\\star Id)(p^k) = \\sum_{d|p^k}f(\\frac{p^k}{d})(d)=\\sum_{d|p^k}f(d)\\frac{p^k}{d}\\]\" width=\"320\" height=\"51\" /> since the the sum can be broken into pairs of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/9/d5940acb75b376ce290f529e98f75af67dc4902d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d,\\frac{p^k}{d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"41\" height=\"41\" /> and the sum remains constant even if you change the order in which each pair appears.\nAs there is not a divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/6585024dc6db82bcfd717e03212be80536d94a83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"17\" height=\"19\" /> that does not divide <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/c/a5cf3da08ae50508e5578698aa5954b4a818d950.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^{k-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"36\" height=\"21\" />, we can say:  \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/6/086e929a41e65d28c931e5ce50b3311b61a9c02a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{d|p^k}f(d)\\frac{p^k}{d}=\\sum_{d|p^k,d\\neq p^k}f(d)\\frac{p^k}{d}+f(p^k)=p*\\sum_{d|p^{k-1}}f(d)\\frac{p^{k-1}}{d}+f(p^k)=1\\]\" width=\"538\" height=\"51\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/3/5b3d89ac0e0c1dfaa4757261c5c45d7d80ec0e71.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\because \\sum_{d|p^{k-1}}f(d)\\frac{p^{k-1}}{d}=(f\\star Id)(p^{k-1})=1, p*(f\\star Id)(p^{k-1})+f(p^k)=p(1)+f(p^k)=1\\implies f(p^k)=1-p\\]\" width=\"769\" height=\"51\" /> This is our final identity. We can use this easily if we can show that f is multiplicative. We can do this very easily as below:\n</p><p><br />\nTake <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/e/7fe35ce2f78014de6bf5865fb76445b7e2aab7aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$gcd(a,b)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/6/5a64aba84125b4dd3c6e3c9e5bbcce67821bf0d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a,b\\in\\mathbb{Z^+}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" />.Then, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/b/5ab931f8df4d7443a9fe8fba529ea7574ecf9238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(f\\star Id)(ab) = (1)(1) = ((f\\star Id)(a))((f\\star Id)(b))\\implies (f\\star Id)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"496\" height=\"20\" /> is multiplicative. Since the dirichlet convolution of two  functions is multiplicative if and only if both input functions are multiplicative, f is multiplicative. So:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53b12d1f0d5fbaaf91622409d17d4bebb9a2d779.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(2023)= f(17^2)* f(7) = (-16)(-6) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }} 96$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"386\" height=\"30\" />\n~Stereotypicalmathnerd\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_MOP_2024\">Video Solution by MOP 2024</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by MOP 2024\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://YouTube.com/watch?v=gdhVqdRhMsQ\">https://YouTube.com/watch?v=gdhVqdRhMsQ</a>\n</p><p>~r00tsOfUnity\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Trz8DEmgAtk\">https://youtu.be/Trz8DEmgAtk</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Fyd1hGGHZ8k\">https://youtu.be/Fyd1hGGHZ8k</a>\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A\">2023 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">Problem 21</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">Problem 23</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2023 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017145311\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.069 seconds\nReal time usage: